<h1>Something went wrong</h1>

<div class="callout warn">
  <%# Stripe's own message is shown verbatim. In a SAMPLE that is right: its wording
      is far more actionable than any paraphrase.

      In production it is not. A Stripe validation error can echo the submitted value
      back, so rendering it can put a customer's details on an error page. The main
      app strips Stripe's message for exactly this reason — see
      Fuime::RequirementCollectionService#submit!. %>
  <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0; font: inherit;"><%= h message %></pre>
</div>

<p><a href="/">Back to the dashboard</a></p>
